## 🎮 Discord‑Bot Dashboard – Front‑end Starter Pack  
Below is a **complete, ready‑to‑run** front‑end skeleton (HTML + CSS + JS) that you can drop into a `public/` folder of any static‑host (Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages, etc.).  

It gives you:

| Feature | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| **OAuth2 login** (Discord) | Opens the Discord consent screen, receives the access token in the URL fragment. |
| **Responsive layout** | Mobile‑first, flex‑grid, dark‑mode‑ready. |
| **Bot info cards** | Shows online status, guild count, command usage (placeholder data). |
| **Command list** | Collapsible list of commands with description & usage. |
| **Live‑refresh** | Simple `fetch` to a placeholder `/api/bot-stats` endpoint (you’ll replace it with your real backend). |

> **Note** – The front‑end can’t talk directly to Discord’s API; you’ll need a tiny Node/Express (or any) backend that handles the OAuth2 token exchange and provides the `/api/bot-stats` JSON. The code below shows the contract.

